cy terms (Modifier), measurement/assay heads, generic biochemical descriptions, and isolated symptom-list items. I verify this doesn't conflict with existing entity definitions before finalizing just the list as the output.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Nominal deficit phrases name the disease, including their biomolecule complement:** IF a noun phrase's head is a nominal deficit or loss-of-function term (such as \"deficiency,\" \"absence,\" or \"deficient activity\" used as a noun) and takes a prepositional complement (\"of\" or \"in\") that names a gene, enzyme, or protein as the defective entity, AND the phrase denotes a congenital or inherited deficiency state, THEN label the entire noun phrase, including the prepositional complement, as SpecificDisease. A premodifying biomolecule name before a final deficit head (e.g., \"[enzyme] deficiency\") falls under the same rule.\n  - **Does NOT apply when:**\n    - (a) The deficit term is adjectival or predicative (e.g., \"[enzyme] deficient\"). Label these as Modifier.\n    - (b) The head is a bare measurement, assay, level, or concentration term that lacks a deficit sense. A deficit qualifier on such a head, as in \"deficient activity,\" does count as a deficit head.\n    - (c) The construction is a generic biochemical or mechanistic description with no congenital or inherited deficiency reading.\n    - (d) The item is an isolated symptom in a coordinated presentation list. Such items are outside this pattern and should not be used to widen it.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1887, "output_tokens": 2427, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1993}, "servic